Let me write engine.js in two parts: first constructor/events/flow; second update/render-related methods appended? Could use a single class in one file split across two writes using write then edit append. `write` can't append; `edit` can replace a marker at the end. Approach: write engine.js with class part 1 ending with a marker comment, then `edit` replace marker with remaining methods. Or use shell heredoc append. The edit tool works fine.

Let me write Part A (~15k chars) then Part B via edit with unique anchor.

Part A:
- imports
- class Game constructor + dom refs
- resize/stars
- bind events + input
- audio/mute
- menu/run flow methods
- show/hide helpers
- HUD setup/sync/banner
- startWave/clearWave/die/win/showOver
- pause/quit.

Part B:
- updateMenu/updatePlaying/updateDying/updateAfter
- physics helpers (attach/release, findAnchor, comboMult, hurt, progress, spawn logic)
- loop/frame
- debug.

Let me draft carefully.

Constructor:
```js
constructor() {
 this.canvas=$('stage'); this.ctx=...;
 if (!this.ctx) ...
 this.audio = new AudioEngine();
 this.best = loadNum('naber.best',0);
 this.muted = loadStr('naber.muted','0')==='1';
 this.audio.muted=this.muted;
 this.state='menu';
 this.t=0; this.last=performance.now();
 this.w=0;this.h=0; ...
 this.pointer={x:0,y:0,sx:0,sy:0,active:false};
 this.hover=null;
 this.attached=null;
 this.particles=[]; this.texts=[];
 this.reduceMotion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
 ...
 this.dom = {...}
 this.resize();
 this.buildStars();
 initGlows(this);
 this.setupMenuWorld();
 this.buildHearts();
 this.bind();
 this.syncHud? no hud hidden
 this.updateBestLabels();
 document.body.classList.toggle('muted',this.muted);
 // start loop
 this.frameBound = this.frame.bind(this);
 requestAnimationFrame(this.frameBound);
}
```
Entity init before resize? entityScale set in resize; fine.

setupMenuWorld:
```
this.voidR=ARENA_R;
this.anchors=createAnchors(); updateAnchors(this,0);
this.leeches=[]; this.particles=[]; this.texts=[]; this.shards=[];
for i<6 spawnShard(this) with type cyan
this.player=this.makePlayer();
this.player.x=0;y=-160;vx=140...
this.attached=null; this.ropeLen=0;
this.menuWait=0.4; this.menuHold=1.2;
this.intermission=0;
...
```
makePlayer:
```
{ x:0,y:-190, vx:130, vy:0, angle:0, invuln:0, surge:0, trail:[], look:{x:1,y:0}, fade:1 }
```
In menu, player might collide? stepPlayer(demo=true) skips core/void; demo confinement in updateMenu.

But demo tethers to anchors at 322; if it reels to 58 near anchor, it could drift beyond 430; confinement.

buildHearts: 3 spans into #hearts. Store this.heartEls.

buildStars.

hideAllScreens: menu/pause/over add hidden; remove menu... etc.

`startRun()`:
```
this.audio.init();
this.audio.setMuted(this.muted);
this.audio.startMusic();
this.audio.duck(false);
this.hideScreens();
this.beginRun();
this.state='playing';
```
beginRun:
```
this.score=0; this.wave=1; this.hull=3; this.waveShards=0; this.totalShards=0; this.bestChain=1; this.combo=0;this.comboTimer=0;this.surge? on player
this.voidR=ARENA_R;
this.anchors=createAnchors(); updateAnchors(this,0);
this.shards=[]; this.leeches=[];this.particles=[];this.texts=[];
this.player=make... starting position 0,-200, vx=170.
this.attached=null; ropeLen=0; this.hover=null;
this.intermission=0; this.victoryQueued=false; this.clearCount=0;
this.shardTimer=0.6; this.leechTimer=4; this.lastReleaseAt=-99; this.t=0;
this.shake=0;this.flash=0;this.flashColor=...;this.hitstop=0;this.deathT=0;
this.hudTimer=0; this.hintTimer=9; this.pointer.active=false;
this.buildHearts(); // reset classes
this.startWave(1,true);
spawn 3 shards;
this.showHud();
```
Note `this.t=0` resets visuals; anchors update with t.

startWave(n, initial=false):
```
this.wave=n; spec=WAVES[n-1]; this.waveGoal=spec.goal; this.waveShards=0; this.intermission=0; this.leechTimer = initial?5:3.5; this.shardTimer=0.2;
this.voidR = Math.min(ARENA_R, this.voidR); // remains
for leeches remove? clearWave already cleared
this.showBanner(`WAVE ${String(n).padStart(2,'0')}`, spec.name, spec.sub);
this.audio.warn? no
this.syncHud(true);
```
Wait intermission ended and void reset. startWave should ensure void start at 500? clearWave sets intermission and void lerp; startWave after 2.6s; void may be 470. Set voidR = ARENA_R? The void resets fully for a breather. Yes: in startWave, `this.voidR = ARENA_R`. This makes each wave start fresh; good. But during intermission void recedes visually, then full reset. Fine.

`progress()`: waveGoal ? clamp(waveShards/waveGoal) : 0.

`clearWave()`:
```
if (this.intermission>0) return;
const n=this.wave; const bonus=400+n*150;
this.score+=bonus;
this.intermission=2.8;
this.victoryQueued = n>=WAVES.length;
this.audio.waveClear();
this.showBanner('WAVE CLEAR', `${WAVES[n-1].name} SECURED`, `+${bonus} · HULL REPAIRED`);
if (this.hull<3) {this.hull++; this.pulseHearts();}
this.player.invuln=Math.max(this.player.invuln,3);
// clear leeches
for l: burst; l.dead
this.leeches=[]
// burst
shock(0,0,lime,400,1.2)
burst(player...)
this.flash=0.35; color lime; shake
this.combo +=? no
this.syncHud()
```
During intermission update: void recedes, player can move; no damage? set invuln. At intermission end → if victoryQueued → this.win() else startWave(wave+1).
But `this.intermission` set 2.8, decremented in updatePlaying. In `updatePlaying`, if intermission >0: skip void shrink and spawns, but still player/shards/leeches. Leeches cleared. At end call next.

`win()`:
```
this.state='victory';
this.attached=null;
this.audio.victory(); this.audio.duck(true);
// update best
this.showResults(true);
```
showResults(victory):
```
const newBest = this.score>this.best;
if (newBest) {this.best=this.score; save('naber.best',this.best);}
update labels;
set texts;
over.classList.remove('hidden');
hud hide; combo/surge/hint hide
pause screen hidden; menu hidden;
state = victory?'victory':'over';
```
Need buttons: again, menu.

`die()`:
```
this.state='dying'; this.deathT=1.5; this.attached=null; this.audio.gameOver(); this.audio.duck(true);
this.player.invuln=999? no, fade.
this.burst...
this.shake=30; this.flash=1; this.flashColor=magenta;
this.hide hud? keep until results.
```
updateDying: t += dt*0.5; update particles/texts/shake/flash; deathT -= dt? Use raw? The main frame passes dt; updateDying(dt): this.t += dt*0.45; ... this.deathT -= dt; player fade; if deathT<=0 → showResults(false).
Also allow skip on click? maybe add listeners for Enter to show results instantly? Not needed.

Set `this.player.fade = clamp(deathT/1.5,0,1)`? If dying from 1.5 to 0, fade to 0. Render needs fade. Let's patch render to use p.fade. Also hide player after 0.4 maybe. Actually updateDying player drift with gravity? Step physics would cause movement. We can just leave the player static and fade out. Add particles.

showResults(false) uses state 'over'. `this.audio.gameOver` already started at die; don't restart. showResults sets state.

best update only once; guard.

`hud best` shows saved best.

Pause/resume.

Return to menu:
```
this.state='menu';
this.hideScreens(); menu show;
this.dom.hud class hidden, combo hidden...
this.audio.stopMusic? Keep ambient; audio.duck(false); audio.startMusic();
this.setupMenuWorld(); // reset demo
this.updateBestLabels();
```
setupMenuWorld uses t? Leave t as is. Empty particles.

Quit from pause: returnToMenu.

Buttons via addEventListener.

Keyboard:
```
keydown e:
 if (e.code==='KeyM') toggleMute
 if (e.repeat) return
 if state playing && (code Space) → press; preventDefault
 if (state playing && (Escape/KeyP)) pause
 if paused && (Escape/KeyP) resume
 if menu && (Enter/Space) startRun
 if over/victory && (Enter/Space/KeyR) startRun; Escape → menu
keyup space → release
```
Also prevent scrolling space.

Pointerdown on canvas starts; if the game state is playing. `pointerup` global release.

Note that on desktop, clicking pause button etc. won't reach canvas (HUD buttons). Good.

`updatePointer(e)`:
```
const r=this.canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
const sx=e.clientX-r.left, sy=e.clientY-r.top;
this.pointer.sx=sx;...
this.pointer.x=(sx-this.cx)/this.scale; ...
this.pointer.active=true;
```
On touch, the finger's world position may be outside arena; fine.

`hover` update: if pointer.active && state playing → this.hover=this.findAnchor(...).

But hover picking nearest to player when pointer inactive could confuse; require active. On touch, after pointerup the finger remains active; hover would stay and show a dotted line. Set pointer.active=false on pointerup? For mouse, we want hover highlight even when not pressed. Keep active for mouse moves. On pointerup, don't reset. The dotted line only shows when not attached; after release it may show a line to the nearest anchor. That's a nice aim hint. Fine.

`findAnchor(wx,wy,requireRange=true)`.

`attach(anchor)`:
```
this.attached=anchor; this.ropeLen=Math.max(90, Math.hypot(...)); this.attachTime=0; this.audio.attach(); burst; shock; this.shake=2; this.hover=anchor; this.dom.hint hidden; this.hasTethered=true;
```
`releaseTether(silent=false)`:
```
if (!this.attached) return;
const p=this.player; 
p.vx*=1.075; p.vy*=1.075; const sp=...; if (sp>0) {p.vx += p.vx/sp*65; ...}
this.attached=null; this.ropeLen=0; this.lastReleaseAt=this.t; this.cooldown=0.1;
if (!silent){this.audio.release(); shock; burst; this.attachTime=0}
else {this.attached=null...}
```
When paused, detach silently? Pausing while attached would drop tether and the player flies when resuming; instead freeze attached and keep it; on resume still attached. Better: don't release on pause. Input release on blur while playing should release though. Keep pause freezes state. On pause, set pressed false but if attached, it remains (holding state lost); on resume, pointer up already happened so attached remains forever? The player can press? press returns if attached. Add: on resume, if attached and no pointer down → release? Simpler: don't release on pause; when resuming, player remains attached with reel continuing automatically; that's a benefit but okay. Actually auto-reel continues only while update runs. On resume it reels; no input needed. Fine, minor.

But window pointerup while paused: releaseTether checks state? It could release while paused. Add `if (this.state!=='playing') return;` in releaseTether triggered by input, but pause calls no release. Define inputRelease() guard state. `releaseTether` internal.

Blur → release only when playing.

Pause overlay z20 covers canvas; pointerup might hit overlay but window listener still fires; guard.

`comboMult()`.

`hurt(source,x,y)`:
```
if (state!=='playing') return;
const p=this.player;
if (p.invuln>0||p.surge>0) return;
this.hull--; ...
if (this.hull<=0) {this.die(); return;} else ...
```
spawn burst at player or source.

`updateHearts` updates classes.

Loop:
```
frame(now) {
 const raw=(now-this.last)/1000; this.last=now;
 const dt=Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, raw));
 if (this.state==='playing' && this.hitstop>0) {this.hitstop-=dt;} else if (this.state==='playing') this.updatePlaying(dt);
 else if (this.state==='dying') this.updateDying(dt);
 else if (this.state==='menu') this.updateMenu(dt);
 else if (this.state==='over'||this.state==='victory') this.updateAfter(dt);
 renderGame(this);
 requestAnimationFrame(this.frameBound);
}
```
Hitstop should freeze but flash/shake update maybe. Just return early but decrement; render static. Fine.

Paused/over: render.

Note `this.last` initialized; tab hidden long → clamped.

`updateAfter`: t+=dt; update anchors? yes slow; particles; texts; flash; shake; player? not drawn maybe (over). For victory, draw player idle? Keep player visible in victory behind overlay. Fine; state not playing, no input.

Menu update and startRun.

In menu, draw player: patch render later.

`updateMenu(dt)`:
```
this.t+=dt;
updateAnchors
// player AI
const p=this.player;
if (!this.attached) {
 this.menuWait-=dt;
 if (this.menuWait<=0) {
   const near=this.anchors.filter(a=>dist(p,a)<=ROPE_MAX*0.9);
   if(near.length){const a=near[randInt(0,near.length-1)]; this.attached=a; this.ropeLen=Math.max(90,dist...); this.menuHold=rand(0.7,1.4); burst...}
   else this.menuWait=0.2;
 }
} else {
 this.menuHold-=dt; this.attachTime+=dt;
 if(this.menuHold<=0) { releaseTether(true); this.menuWait=rand(0.25,0.7); }
}
stepPlayer(this,dt,true);
// confinement
const d=hypot(p.x,p.y);
if(d>430){ p.vx -= p.x/d*300*dt ... }? Simpler: if d>460: scale position to 460; reflect velocity inward *0.6.
if (d>470) {...}
// look toward pointer? use nearest shard for eye
p.look = toward pointer if pointer.active else velocity
p.invuln=0;p.surge=0;
updateShards? For menu, drift only and no pickup; write manual loop: s.rot+=...; s.x+=...; clamp to voidR. Could call updateShards which would collect and score! Bad. Write simple ambient drift.
updateParticles, texts, flash/shake decay.
// keep shards count 6: shardTimer...
```
Menu shards drift slowly and respawn. Simplest: no shards in menu? But visual interest. Keep 7; if none (never) spawn. Positions fixed initial; drift. Add slow rotation around center: give vx/vy initial tangential; they'll drift out and then... clamp/bounce. Write custom clamp.

Also updateHover? No.

For demo release, `releaseTether(true)` sets this.lastReleaseAt etc. Fine.

Autopilot attach should set audio? silent (no audio in menu) — audio.attach would sound; avoid: set directly instead of attach method. Write helper `attachMenu(a)` or call attach then audio noise (could be nice subtle). Better silent. Implement in updateMenu manually.

`updatePlaying(dt)`:
```
this.t += dt;
this.shake = Math.max(0, this.shake - dt*55);
this.flash = Math.max(0, this.flash - dt*2.6);
this.surgeWash = Math.max(0, this.surgeWash - dt*1.4);
this.hitstop... handled
this.pointer...
this.updateHover();
updateAnchors
if (this.intermission>0) {
  this.intermission -= dt;
  this.voidR = lerp(this.voidR, ARENA_R, 1-Math.exp(-dt*2.0));
  if (this.intermission<=0) { if(this.victoryQueued) this.win(); else this.startWave(this.wave+1); }
} else {
  const spec=WAVES[this.wave-1];
  const factor=clamp((this.voidR-352)/148,0,1);
  this.voidR -= spec.shrink*factor*dt*(this.player.surge>0?0.5:1);
  // spawns
  this.shardTimer-=dt;
  const cap=6+Math.floor(this.wave/2);
  if (this.shardTimer<=0 && this.shards.length<cap) { spawnShard(this); this.shardTimer=rand(0.55,0.95); }
  // leeches
  this.leechTimer-=dt;
  if (spec.leeches>0 && this.leechTimer<=0 && this.leeches.length<spec.leeches) {spawnLeech(this); this.leechTimer=rand(6,9);}
  // initial leech quicker
}
// timers
if combo>0 { comboTimer-=dt; if<=0 combo=0 }
if player.surge>0 {surge-=dt; if<=0 {surge=0; player.invuln=Math.min(player.invuln,0.6)}}
player.invuln = max(0, invuln-dt)
cooldown = max...
hintTimer...
// move
stepPlayer(this,dt,false);
// after movement: update look toward pointer
...
updateShards, updateLeeches, particles, texts
// close the loop: check core? already.
// hint/edge
if hintTimer>0 and hasTethered → hide
if hintTimer<=? hide at 8s
// hud timer
// danger warning
this.edgeOn = dist(player) > voidR-120
this.dom.edgeWarning.classList.toggle('on', ...)
// audio intensity
this.audio.tick(clamp(this.wave/8*0.75 + this.combo/24,0,1))
// auto-hide hint
```
Need `hasTethered` flag reset per run.

When intermission, don't spawn. But still update shards (collect counts?) Wave clear already done; waveShards may exceed goal; next wave resets. Fine. Could allow collection during intermission to add score; okay.

Wave clear inside collectShard triggers intermission; and updatePlaying later same frame decrements it a tiny bit. Fine.

`startWave` during update; banner.

Hint hide: DOM `.hidden` class. Show at start of run, hide after 9s or first tether. Then possibly show again? no.

Also show "SLING" cue? no.

`updateDying`:
```
this.t+=dt*0.5; this.deathT-=dt;
this.shake*=...; flash decays; particles; texts;
if (player) player.fade = clamp(deathT/1.2,0,1) — wait initial deathT=1.5, fade stays 1 until deathT<1.2 then fades. 
if(deathT<=0) this.showResults(false);
```
During dying, don't move player.

`updateAfter`:
```
this.t += dt*0.6; updateAnchors; updateParticles; updateTexts; shake/flash
```
But if state 'over', best already saved.

`showResults(victory)`:
```
this.state = victory?'victory':'over';
this.attached=null;
this.hideHud();
this.hideScreens();
// update best
if (this.score>this.best) { ... newBest }
set DOM texts
this.dom.over.classList.remove('hidden')
this.audio.duck(true)
```
For victory audio already played at win.
Title innerHTML: victory ? 'VOID<br>NABBED' : 'EATEN BY<br>THE VOID'
kicker: victory ? 'ALL EIGHT WAVES CLEARED' : 'RUN TERMINATED'
new best class hidden toggled.
again button label maybe "AGAIN" both.
`over-wave`: this.wave; `over-shards`: totalShards; `over-chain`: `×${bestChain}`.
`final-score`: fmt(score) animated? Add count-up? Could animate score in results via requestAnimationFrame; maybe simple CSS pop. Skip count-up (adds polish but time). Maybe add a quick JS count-up using interval? Not needed.

`hideScreens()` adds hidden to menu, pause, over.

`showMenu()`.

Hearts: buildHearts fills spans each (3) and updateHearts sets classes.

`pulseHearts` on heal: add class pulse to last heart; remove after animation (setTimeout).

HUD elements mapping using document.getElementById. Use helper `el(id)`.

`syncHud(force)`:
```
if (!force && this.hudTimer>0) return;
this.hudTimer=0.09;
...
```
But when called from world collect each time, it would throttle? Actually check timer. Use force for immediate. Simpler: set a `hudDirty=true`, and in updatePlaying sync at 10Hz. world calls g.syncHud() → set dirty. Implement syncHud as immediate writes with throttling:
```
syncHud(force=false) {
 if (!force && this.t - this.lastHudSync < 0.08) return;
 this.lastHudSync=this.t;
 ... writes
}
```
Score updates within 0.08s fine.

Values from state. Hearts: update every sync (cheap class check). Combo etc.

Formatting score with commas via fmt.

Wave progress: goal.

Surge: show if player.surge>0; fill scaleX(surge/6.5). Might be hidden in menu.

Combo show if combo>0 && !intermission? keep.

Edge warning updated separately.

`updateBestLabels`: menu-best, hud best.

`showBanner`: guard elements.

Toggle mute: audio.init? If not initialized, a click should initialize (gesture) and then mute; but playing audio immediately could be unexpected. Only init if state playing? Simpler: toggle state, save, apply if ready. The first Play initializes with muted state. Add `if (this.audio.ready) this.audio.setMuted(this.muted)`.

`beginRun` audio.init.

Note: AudioEngine `init` sets master gain based on `this.muted` which we set in constructor before init. Good.

`findAnchor`: use entityScale? no.

`attach`: if anchor consumed? still allow.

`updateHover`: only when playing and pointer active:
```
this.hover = this.attached ? this.attached : this.findAnchor();
```
But findAnchor uses pointer and returns nearest by pointer. For showing candidate, yes. However auto-target nearest in range means hover always shows an anchor even when the pointer isn't near; could be helpful. But then the dotted line always visible → clutter. Require pointer distance < 230 OR pointer is down? Let's show hover only if the pointer is within 260 of an anchor, otherwise null. Attach still auto-selects nearest. This makes hover a true "you're aiming at this" signal.

Implement `findAnchorForHover`: pick pointer-nearest within 220 and in range; else null. The dotted line appears when aiming. On touch, pressing anywhere near player might not be near any anchor; press auto-selects nearest. Fine.

Also highlight all anchors in range via their alpha.

`findAnchor` implementation:
```
let byPtr=null,bp=Infinity;
for a active: const dp=Math.hypot(a.x-wx,a.y-wy); if(dp<bp){bp=dp;byPtr=a}
const p=this.player;
if (!byPtr) return null;
if (bp<230 && Math.hypot(byPtr.x-p.x,byPtr.y-p.y)<=ROPE_MAX) return byPtr;
let best=null,bd=ROPE_MAX;
for a: const d=...; if(d<bd){bd=d;best=a}
return best;
```
If all anchors out of range, null.

Hover:
```
if (!this.pointer.active) return null;
const a = pointer-nearest with dPtr<230 and in range; return a;
```
During press, we can set hover=attached for render.

`pressTether`:
```
if (!this.player || this.attached || this.state!=='playing') return;
if (this.cooldown>0) return;
const a=this.findAnchor(this.pointer.x,this.pointer.y);
if(!a){ this.cooldown=.25; floatText(player...,'OUT OF REACH',dim); this.audio.warn(); return; }
this.attach(a);
```
`attach`:
```
this.attached=a; this.ropeLen=Math.max(90,dist); this.attachTime=0;
this.audio.attach(); burst/schock; this.shake=2.5;
this.hasTethered=true;
if hint visible hide
```
Note: pointer might not be active if keyboard space pressed. findAnchor still uses pointer coords (0,0 default) → selects by nearest. It's fine. For keyboard, aim is nearest anchor.

`releaseTether(input)`:
```
if (!this.attached) return;
const p=this.player;
const sp=hypot;
p.vx*=1.07; p.vy*=1.07;
if(sp>1){ p.vx+=p.vx/sp*55; p.vy+=p.vy/sp*55;}
...
this.audio.release(); shock at p; burst
this.attached=null; this.ropeLen=0; this.cooldown=0.06; this.lastReleaseAt=this.t;
```
Cap speed.

If stroke is vertical and player is at anchor... boost radial? If velocity points toward anchor (radial), release flings toward anchor — fine.

Maybe add tangential release even if velocity is radial? Not necessary.

`updateHearts` after damage: class pulse on the lost heart? Use pulse on remaining? Add class 'pulse' to all. Remove after 500ms via setTimeout.

Potential issue: starting state menu, HUD hidden but hearts built. `buildHearts` at constructor.

`startWave` shows banner; the banner is absolutely positioned over the game; fine.

`showBanner` uses innerHTML? textContent for security (local only). Use textContent.

`hint` text: update for mobile? same.

`startRun` hides menu; shows HUD; the hint shown in beginRun.

`menu` is initially visible; state menu. Need a "click Play" gesture. Bind play button.

`audio.init` only on button click. Key Enter also user gesture → okay.

On mute toggle before start, under overlay not accessible. Fine.

`startRun` also hides banner? showBanner wave 1 after.

`beginRun` sets `this.dom.hint` visible.

`this.dom.combo` hide; surge hide.

`renderGame` uses state to decide player; patch.

Time to write.

One more detail: `this.syncHud` called from world during menu? Only in collect/pop which don't happen in menu. Fine.

`hurt` called from stepPlayer → may call die → state changes; subsequent update logic still runs but check.

`this.audio.tone` referenced in world for core bounce; AudioEngine has tone method. Fine.

Now careful with `this.entityScale` in world collisions — defined in resize.

`this.voidR` initial set.

`this.player.surge` etc.

`this.wave` initial 1.

`menu` update uses `releaseTether(true)` which sets lastReleaseAt; fine. `releaseTether` also plays audio if !silent; menu passes true.

Menu autopilot should pick anchors that keep it on screen. Use all.

Confinement code:
```
const d=Math.hypot(p.x,p.y);
if (d>440) {
  const nx=p.x/d, ny=p.y/d;
  p.x=nx*440; p.y=ny*440;
  const vr=p.vx*nx+p.vy*ny;
  if (vr>0){ p.vx-=nx*vr*1.4; p.vy-=ny*vr*1.4; }
}
