But at attach rope=d, d==rope. Each frame after integration, gravity moves inward/outward; the constraint sets the position exactly. Then velocity's radial component is removed. This effectively makes a rigid circular pendulum. However, when reeling, rope decreases; the position is set to the shorter radius, and the radial component removed. Tangential speed stays. Good.

Potential issue: if the player is near the anchor (d=0), direction undefined; but rope min 118 keeps d=118. On attach, d could be < 118 if the player is close to an anchor; ropeLen = max(88, d) currently uses 88 < ROPE_MIN. Should be max(ROPE_MIN+8, d) to avoid weird. Set pressTether ropeLen = max(ROPE_MIN + 10, dist). Menu too.

But if the anchor is within 118 of the player, attaching snaps them outward to 128; fine.

Implement.

